==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂ep-|*ǵʰes-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ota|آبدست}} (modern {{cog|tr|abdest}}), from {{bor|en|fa|آبدست|tr=âbdast}}, compound of {{m|fa|آب|tr=âb|t=water}} and {{m|fa|دست|tr=dast|t=hand}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɑb.dɛst/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-abdest.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑbdɛst|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{senseid|en|ritual}} {{lb|en|Islam}} The [[Islamic]] act of [[wash]]ing parts of the body using [[water]] for ritual [[prayer]]s and for handling and reading the [[Qur'an]].
#: {{synonyms|en|wudu}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|wazukhana}} (place where wudu is performed, South Asia)

